$ jailops remote add known https://<addr> --token tok --fingerprint <fingerprint>
remote/known added (now the current remote)
connected to tls-host (version fake), seen as trusted

$ jailops remote add sock unix:/run/other.sock --switch
remote/sock added (now the current remote)
! warning: saved, but the server could not be reached: Get "http://jailops.local/api/v1": dial unix /run/other.sock: connect: no such file or directory

$ jailops remote list
    NAME    TARGET                               AUTH           HOST   SOURCE
    local   unix:/var/run/jailops/jailops.sock   root only      -      built-in
    known   https://<addr>              token+pinned   -      user
*   sock    unix:/run/other.sock                 root only      -      user

$ jailops remote switch known
now using remote known

